WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.413
Marjo Seki is an author and a teacher of Japanese cooking, based in Kouvola, Finland.

00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:11.176
I designed and built a new website for Marjo through my company, Findaco.

00:00:12.626 --> 00:00:15.250
The site has five pages, in Finnish.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.493
A home page with Marjo's story,

00:00:17.793 --> 00:00:19.759
cooking courses and services,

00:00:20.059 --> 00:00:20.747
books,

00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:22.339
upcoming events,

00:00:22.639 --> 00:00:24.129
and a contact page.

00:00:25.579 --> 00:00:29.574
The look is warm and playful, inspired by Japanese food culture:

00:00:29.874 --> 00:00:31.228
soft colour bubbles,

00:00:31.228 --> 00:00:32.244
rounded photos,

00:00:32.244 --> 00:00:34.952
and clear type that works on any screen,

00:00:34.952 --> 00:00:36.713
from a phone to a desktop.

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.344
The client runs the site without me.

00:00:40.644 --> 00:00:42.993
A small pencil icon opens a login,

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:46.663
and every text and image can then be edited right on the page.

00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:50.310
One button publishes the changes.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.512
The content is saved to GitHub,

00:00:52.812 --> 00:00:54.464
Vercel rebuilds the site,

00:00:54.764 --> 00:00:57.067
and the update is live in about a minute.

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.145
No code, and no git knowledge needed.

00:01:00.595 --> 00:01:04.648
Book orders and course enquiries go through small serverless functions,

00:01:04.648 --> 00:01:06.646
and arrive by email through Resend.

00:01:06.946 --> 00:01:11.021
Passwords and API keys stay on the server, never in the browser.

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:18.001
Under the hood, it is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript, with no framework,

00:01:18.301 --> 00:01:21.158
so it loads fast and stays easy to maintain.

00:01:22.608 --> 00:01:23.341
marjoseki.

00:01:23.341 --> 00:01:27.742
fi — a fast, friendly website that the client owns and runs.
